  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> be the origin and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>Re</mo><mfenced><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is a right angled isosceles triangle with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;as hypotenuse, then which of the following is NOT true?",
    "image": null
  },
